 "title": "Вызов на кулинарный поединок  (Challenge to a Culinary Duel)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "elena": "Елена",
  "eleonora": "Элеонора"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Elena and Eleonora explain that because work is medically forbidden for Viktor Petrovich, Anton was hired and brought his own cooks, firing Barinov's team. Outraged, Chef Barinov challenges the newcomers to a culinary duel for their jobs.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Витя, тебе совсем нельзя нервничать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Тяжёлая работа тебе сейчас противопоказана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Он привёл сюда свою команду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Ты будешь вести общее руководство.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Он всех моих поваров уволил?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Тогда убирайте моё авторское меню!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "И меняйте вообще название ресторана!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Он уволил лучших поваров Москвы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Они готовят намного лучше вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Давай поставим моих против твоих.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "А мне нравится эта идея.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Давайте устроим сегодня честный поединок.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Витя, тебе совсем нельзя нервничать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Vitya, you must not get nervous at all.' Opening up quietly in front of Eleonora, Elena adds \"sovsem\" (\"completely, at all\") so the statement leaves zero room for doubt.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Тяжёлая работа тебе сейчас противопоказана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Heavy work is forbidden for you right now.' Eleonora speaks right away during the talk, keeping the focus on what actually matters here.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Он привёл сюда свою команду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He brought his own team here.' Addressing the team in this beat, Eleonora brings in \"komandu\" (\"team\", from \"komanda\") as the key Russian word here.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Ты будешь вести общее руководство.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You will handle general supervision.' Eleonora counters briskly with a smile, grounding the moment in plain reality.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Он всех моих поваров уволил?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did he fire all of my cooks?' Barinov prompts frankly to see how Eleonora will answer on the spot.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Тогда убирайте моё авторское меню!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Then take away my signature menu!' Emphasizing the menu around Eleonora, Barinov reaches for the Russian word \"avtorskoye\" (\"auteur, signature\", built from \"avtorskiy\") right at the center of the line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "И меняйте вообще название ресторана!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And change the name of the restaurant altogether!' Checking on the name in front of Eleonora, Barinov drops in \"voobshche\" (\"in general, altogether\") to sum up the whole situation at once.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Он уволил лучших поваров Москвы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He fired the best cooks in Moscow.' Barinov speaks up dryly without any doubt, leaving no doubt about where he stands.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Они готовят намного лучше вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They cook much better than you.' Barinov speaks calmly with Eleonora and uses \"gotovyat\" (\"are preparing\", from \"gotovit\") to make the point stick.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Давай поставим моих против твоих.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let us put my guys against yours.' Speaking boldly beside Eleonora, Barinov starts with \"davay\" (\"come on, let's\") to invite Eleonora right into the action.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "А мне нравится эта идея.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I actually like this idea.' Eleonora steps in lightly during the talk, testing Barinov's reaction in the middle of the exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Давайте устроим сегодня честный поединок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let us hold a fair duel today.' Addressing a fair duel to Barinov, Eleonora reaches for the Russian word \"poyedinok\" (\"duel, match\") right at the heart of the line.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Витя, тебе совсем нельзя нервничать.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Тяжёлая работа тебе сейчас противопоказана.",
   "gap": 0.5
